resumegen bundles no fonts and no PDF engine. It invokes Typst
(https://typst.app, Apache License 2.0) as a separate program, and the PDFs
it produces embed subsets of fonts that ship inside the Typst binary: New
Computer Modern by Antonis Tsolomitis (GUST Font License), Libertinus Serif
(SIL Open Font License 1.1), and DejaVu Sans Mono (Bitstream Vera /
public-domain-derived license). All three licenses permit embedding in a
document without placing conditions on that document, so a resume rendered by
this tool carries no license obligation from the fonts.

Third-party Go modules linked into the released binaries are listed with
their full license texts in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

